# Committed template. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in — `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are inlined into the browser bundle; the rest are
# server-side only. Never add the prefix to a secret.
#
# Why any of these are set the way they are — the Console tabs they come from,
# the credentials that deliberately do not appear here, and what breaks if you
# get one wrong — is in docs/AUTH-PLAN.md. Keep the reasoning there, not here.

# The FastAPI adapter (`backend/api/`), read by `src/lib/api/client.ts`.
# Dev default matches `uvicorn api.main:app --reload` run from `backend/`.
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# The agent service, read by `src/app/api/agent/[...path]/route.ts`.
# Dev default matches `python scripts/serve.py` run from `agent/`.
# ⚠️ Loopback is load-bearing: the agent has no authentication of its own, so
# pointing this anywhere else exposes it. See `agent/app.py`'s HOST comment.
AGENT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8002

# ── ThunderID ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Started from deploy/docker-compose.thunderid.yml.

NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_BASE_URL=https://localhost:8090

# Console -> AIsle Gate -> Credentials -> Client ID. Public: the browser needs it
# to be sent to the authorize endpoint, hence NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_CLIENT_ID=

# Console -> AIsle Gate -> Credentials -> Client Secret. Shown once at creation;
# treat as a password. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and never add one - that would
# inline it into the browser bundle.
THUNDERID_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Signs our own session cookie. Not a ThunderID value, and not the client
# secret with a word missing. `openssl rand -base64 32`.
THUNDERID_SECRET=

# Permissions requested on the authorize URL, space-separated. These are the
# resource server's permission strings verbatim - the `Agentic ERP API` resource
# server was registered with delimiter "." precisely so they match the strings
# `services/` passes to `actor.can()` with nothing to translate.
#
# Over-asking is NOT an error here: ThunderID answers 200 with a *narrower*
# scope, and asking for a permission that does not exist returns a token with no
# scope claim at all - indistinguishable from a request that was silently
# gutted. If pages start returning 403, read the token; do not assume this line.
NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_SCOPES=openid product.read product.create product.update stock.adjust

# ⚠️ Four variables that belonged to the abandoned embedded ("Bring Your Own
# UI") setup are deliberately absent, and adding any of them back breaks this
# mode rather than extending it:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_APPLICATION_ID  - only used to look up flow metadata;
#                                           the AIsle Gate app renders the flow
#                                           on ThunderID's own page.
#   THUNDERID_FLOW_SECRET                 - authenticates the embedded flow via
#                                           the `Flow-Secret` header. Nothing
#                                           sends that header any more.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_SIGN_IN_URL     - ⚠️ the dangerous one. <SignInButton>
#                                           does `if (signInUrl) router.push(...)
#                                           else signIn(...)`, so setting it makes
#                                           the button navigate locally and never
#                                           reach the ThunderID gate. Sign-in
#                                           silently stops working.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_SIGN_UP_URL     - there is no self-service signup;
#                                           accounts are created by an admin.
#
# And one that is absent for a subtler reason:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_THUNDERID_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL - despite the name, this is not a
#     landing page. `ThunderIDNextClient.js` resolves it to `afterSignInUrl ??
#     origin`, and `getSignInUrl` then passes it as the OAuth `redirect_uri`. A
#     path such as `/products` is sent verbatim and will not match the
#     Authorized Redirect URI registered in the Console, so authorization fails
#     before the login page renders. Left unset it yields the request origin,
#     which is exactly what the Console has registered. `src/app/page.tsx` sends
#     a signed-in visitor on to /products instead.
#
# See the "AIsle Gate application" block under Gate 24 in docs/AUTH-PLAN.md.

# ⚠️ LOCAL ONLY — disables TLS verification for the whole Node process, because
# ThunderID's dev certificate is self-signed. Must not survive to deployment.
#
# Deliberately COMMENTED OUT. Note the scope: this is not scoped to ThunderID
# the way THUNDERID_VERIFY_TLS is on the backend — it switches off certificate
# checking for *every* HTTPS call this Node process makes, including calls to
# the API. Copying this template must not turn that on silently. Put it in your
# own untracked .env.local instead.
# NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0
